---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { company, contact, commitments, compliance, hubs, cycle } from '../data/company';
---
<Base
  title="Company · About Zanzi Logistics"
  description="Zanzi Logistics is a South African freight, warehousing and customs operator running its own depots in Johannesburg, Cape Town and Durban. How we operate, what we commit to, and the cover we carry."
  ref="ZL-04"
  refName="Company"
>

  <header class="page-hero">
    <div class="container hero-stack">
      <div class="data-strip">
        <span class="data"><strong>Ref ZL-04</strong> &middot; Company</span>
        <span class="data">{company.legalName}</span>
        <span class="data">Est. {company.founded}</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="display">A carrier that<br /><em>answers</em> the phone.</h1>
      <p class="page-sub">
        Zanzi Logistics is a South African freight operator. We run our own
        depots, our own vehicles and our own customs desk &mdash; because the
        moment a job is handed to a stranger, nobody can tell you where your
        freight is.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <div class="hazard" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <!-- ═══ The company ═══ -->
  <section>
    <div class="container about-grid">
      <div class="rv">
        <div class="sec-ref"><span class="data">A &middot; The company</span></div>
        <h2 class="display">Built around one<br />ordinary <em>complaint.</em></h2>
      </div>

      <div class="rv about-body">
        <p>
          Every business that moves freight has the same story. The load was
          collected late. Nobody could say where it was. The invoice came in
          higher than the quote, with a line item nobody could explain. And the
          person who sold you the service was never available once the truck
          was on the road.
        </p>
        <p>
          Zanzi Logistics was set up to run the opposite way. Every account has
          a named controller who books the load, watches it, and calls you
          before you have to call them. Every rate is issued in writing with the
          surcharges spelled out. And every leg we can run ourselves, we do
          &mdash; own vehicles, own depots, own customs entries.
        </p>
        <p>
          We are not the biggest carrier in the country, and there are loads we
          will turn down because we cannot do them properly. That is the trade.
          What you get instead is a carrier small enough that the person
          answering your call already knows which truck your pallets are on.
        </p>

        <div class="pull">
          <p class="pull-q">
            The freight industry does not have a truck problem. It has a
            telling-you-what-is-happening problem.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══ Commitments (black) ═══ -->
  <section id="commitments" class="ink-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="sec-head rv">
        <div class="sec-ref"><span class="data">B &middot; How we operate</span></div>
        <h2 class="display">Four things we<br /><em>will not</em> get wrong.</h2>
        <p class="sub">
          These are not aspirations. They are the terms we work to, and you
          should hold us to every one of them.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="commit-grid rv-group">
        {commitments.map((c) => (
          <div class="commit">
            <span class="data commit-ref">{c.ref}</span>
            <h3>{c.title}</h3>
            <p>{c.body}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══ The cycle recap ═══ -->
  <section class="dim">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="sec-head rv">
        <div class="sec-ref"><span class="data">C &middot; The operating cycle</span></div>
        <h2 class="display">Same four steps,<br />every <em>load.</em></h2>
        <p class="sub">
          One pallet to Polokwane or a full trailer to Lusaka &mdash; the
          process does not change, and neither does who is accountable for it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <ol class="cyc-list rv-group">
        {cycle.map((c) => (
          <li class="cyc-row">
            <span class="data cyc-step">{c.step}</span>
            <div class="cyc-body">
              <h3>{c.name}</h3>
              <p>{c.desc}</p>
            </div>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══ Compliance ═══ -->
  <section id="compliance">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="sec-head rv">
        <div class="sec-ref"><span class="data">D &middot; Cover &amp; compliance</span></div>
        <h2 class="display">The <em>boring</em> part<br />that matters.</h2>
        <p class="sub">
          Nobody asks about insurance until something has already gone wrong.
          Ask now &mdash; and ask every carrier quoting you the same question.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="table-scroll rv">
        <table class="manifest">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col">Item</th>
              <th scope="col">Position</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {compliance.map((c) => (
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">{c.item}</th>
                <td>{c.detail}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <div class="reg-block rv">
        <dl class="reg">
          <div class="reg-cell"><dt class="data">Registered name</dt><dd>{company.legalName}</dd></div>
          <div class="reg-cell"><dt class="data">Registration no.</dt><dd>{company.regNo}</dd></div>
          <div class="reg-cell"><dt class="data">VAT no.</dt><dd>{company.vatNo}</dd></div>
          <div class="reg-cell"><dt class="data">Head office</dt><dd>{hubs[0].address}</dd></div>
        </dl>
        <p class="reg-note">
          Certificates, insurance schedules and our standard trading conditions
          are available on request &mdash; email
          <a class="link" href={`mailto:${contact.email}`}>{contact.email}</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══ CTA ═══ -->
  <section class="drench">
    <div class="container rv-group">
      <div class="data-strip cta-strip">
        <span class="data">Named controller</span>
        <span class="data">Written rates</span>
        <span class="data">Bad news early</span>
      </div>
      <h2 class="display cta-title">Try us on<br />one <em>load.</em></h2>
      <p class="cta-sub">
        You do not have to move your whole account. Give us a single
        consignment and judge us on how that one goes.
      </p>
      <div class="cta-actions">
        <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-ink">Get a quote <span class="arr">&rarr;</span></a>
        <a href="/services" class="btn btn-ghost-red">See all services</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</Base>

<style>
  /* ── The company ── */
  .about-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 0.85fr 1.15fr;
    gap: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 4rem);
    align-items: start;
  }
  .about-body p {
    font-size: 1.02rem;
    line-height: 1.85;
    color: var(--steel);
    margin-bottom: 1.4rem;
  }
  .pull {
    margin-top: 2.2rem;
    border-left: 4px solid var(--red);
    padding: 0.4rem 0 0.4rem 1.6rem;
  }
  .pull-q {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 2.4vw, 1.7rem);
    line-height: 1.25;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
  @media (max-width: 900px) { .about-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }

  /* ── Commitments ── */
  .commit-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2.5rem) clamp(2rem, 4vw, 4rem);
  }
  .commit { border-top: 1px solid var(--rule-on-ink-strong); padding-top: 1.3rem; }
  .commit-ref { color: var(--red-bright); font-weight: 600; }
  .commit h3 { margin: 0.5rem 0 0.7rem; }
  .commit p { font-size: 0.94rem; line-height: 1.75; color: var(--mist-on-ink); }
  @media (max-width: 760px) { .commit-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }

  /* ── Cycle list ── */
  .cyc-list { list-style: none; border-top: 2px solid var(--red); }
  .cyc-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 4rem 1fr;
    gap: 1rem 1.5rem;
    padding: 1.6rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .cyc-step { color: var(--red-deep); font-weight: 600; padding-top: 0.35rem; }
  .cyc-body h3 { margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  .cyc-body p { font-size: 0.96rem; line-height: 1.75; color: var(--steel); }
  @media (max-width: 600px) { .cyc-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0.4rem; } }

  /* ── Registration block ── */
  .reg-block { margin-top: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem); }
  .reg {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule-strong);
    background: var(--paper-raised);
  }
  .reg-cell { padding: 1rem 1.1rem; border-right: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  .reg-cell:last-child { border-right: none; }
  .reg-cell dt { margin-bottom: 0.4rem; }
  .reg-cell dd {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .reg-note { margin-top: 1.2rem; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--steel); }
  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    .reg { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
    .reg-cell:nth-child(2n) { border-right: none; }
    .reg-cell:nth-child(-n+2) { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  }
  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    .reg { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .reg-cell { border-right: none; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
    .reg-cell:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
  }

  /* ── CTA ── */
  .cta-title {
    margin-top: clamp(1.6rem, 3.5vw, 2.4rem);
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 7vw, 5.2rem);
  }
  .cta-sub { margin-top: 1.2rem; font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; max-width: 48ch; }
  .cta-actions { display: flex; gap: 1rem; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 2.2rem; }
</style>
